A thread that may no longer run stays on the queue it waited on.
A thread unbound while it waited would still take turns;
a thread names a queue only while its account and binding put it on one.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-work test qemu-replay
Report: a thread names a queue it is not for

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -205,7 +205,7 @@ static void thread_settle(struct thread *t)
     wake_stale = true;
     account_refill(t);
     uint8_t queue = thread_queue(t, t->balance);
-    if (queue != t->queue) {
+    if (queue != QUEUE_NONE && queue != t->queue) {
         if (t->queue != QUEUE_NONE) {
             ring_remove(queue_head(t->queue), t);
         }
